Z||000000||Zorba||12-19-2000||12:59 PM||||I noticed some small hairline cracks on one of my front tire sidewalls? is this reason to think it will blow out? The cracks are alongside the rim area.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Old Lar||12-19-2000||02:15 PM||||Dry rot.  I replaced my tires when they did that.  I also had cracking in between the tread and other places on the side walls.  Firestone Firehawks 4 years old and 20000 miles.  I didn't want to take chances.||||reg||3
Z||000002||Oreif||12-19-2000||02:52 PM||||Eventually it will cause slow leaks first. The tire has dry rot. Getting new tires will be a world of difference. Usually dry rotted tires become harder and traction/handling suffers.||||reg||1
Z||000003||mrfiero||12-19-2000||03:13 PM||||The original GT+4's on my 16K mile '88 GT are starting to do this.  Unfortunately they don't make these tires anymore, so I'm stuck (I am keeping this GT bone stock).<P>Oreif is right.....if this is a daily driver then replace the tires.  Your handling will greatly improve.||||reg||1
Z||000004||fropuff||12-19-2000||06:18 PM||||mrfiero: I know that Goodyear still makes the +4s.  I saw them in an ad this weekend.  Sears or something like that. <P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters are for those who are worried about being caught.||||reg||1
